-- [[Improvement - Most species outside the original 351 have no Egg Group data]]: full
-- wipe-and-replace of pokedex_egg_groups from PokeAPI (this app's own 14 groups map 1:1 onto
-- PokeAPI's 15 -- the extra `no-eggs` correctly contributes zero rows, same "zero rows = can't
-- breed" convention already used for Legendaries). Generated by a one-off script (scratchpad,
-- not committed) -- see the FR's own Notes for the exact crosswalk/name-matching approach.

-- "Wartorle" (409) and "Wiggytuff" (595) were assumed to be simple typos blocking slug resolution --
-- turned out on closer look to be genuine DUPLICATE rows of the already-correctly-spelled "Wartortle"
-- (1088) and "Wigglytuff" (774) (identical sprite_code/base-stat blocks, confirmed via a stat-twin
-- scan across the whole table), not just misspellings. Renaming them here would collide with
-- pokedex.name's own unique constraint -- deliberately NOT renamed in this migration; tracked
-- separately as [[Bug - Wartortle and Wigglytuff have duplicate pokedex rows under misspelled names]]
-- since merging/removing a duplicate species needs checking real Pokemon/item references first, not a
-- decision to make inside an Egg Group migration. Their `pokedex_id`s still get real egg-group rows
-- below (matched by their real species identity, not their name) -- only the name-cleanup is deferred.

delete from pokedex_egg_groups;

